        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U1 INA219AIDCNR: pin 8 SDA (net I2C2_SDA_FCC), pin 6 A1 (tied to GND)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Current/voltage sensor | Hades (top sheet) | TI INA219AIDCNR, I2C addr 0x40, across R1 = 10 mΩ shunt"}
      ],
      "impact": "The I2C data line is connected to the address pin A1 instead of SDA, and the real SDA pin is grounded. The INA219 will not communicate on I2C and the address will be incorrect, disabling current/voltage sensing.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a pin-mapping error on the INA219 current/voltage sensor: the SDA and A1 pins are swapped relative to the standard INA219AIDCNR pinout, which would prevent I2C communication and break the current/voltage sensing function."
}

